{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.Clausen","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.Clausen","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrability.LogMeromorphic","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral.FundThmCalculus","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Group.FunctionSeries","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.PSeries","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.SmoothSeries","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals.LogTrigonometric","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.AbelLimit","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.LogBounds","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SumIntegralComparisons","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller"],"declarations":53,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.hasDerivAt_cl_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.hasDerivAt_cl_2","kind":"theorem","line":1488,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L1488-L1494","doc":"**The series Clausen's derivative** `Cl_2'(θ) = -log(2 sin(θ/2))` for\n`θ ∈ (0, 2π)` — the derivative the filler flagged as needing Fourier\ninfrastructure, now machine-proved (`hasDerivAt_Cl_2_series`). Dual-purpose: `V'(θ)` of\n`rem:dilog-saddle-regime`, zero at the `θ = π/3` saddle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Cl_2_duplication","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Cl_2_duplication","kind":"theorem","line":1476,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L1476-L1486","doc":"**B1, series side (sorry-free).** `Cl₂(2θ) = 2·Cl₂(θ) − 2·Cl₂(π − θ)` on\n`(0, π)`, via the series↔integral bridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.clausen_duplication","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.clausen_duplication","kind":"theorem","line":1413,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L1413-L1474","doc":"**Borromean brick B1 — the Clausen duplication formula (sorry-free).**\n`clausen(2θ) = 2·clausen(θ) − 2·clausen(π − θ)` on `(0, π)`: both sides\nhave derivative `−2·log(2 sin θ)` (the sine duplication\n`2 sin θ = (2 sin(θ/2))·(2 sin((π−θ)/2))`), and agree at `θ = π/2`\n(`clausen π = 0`). Closes the functional-equation gap the Clausen filler\nlisted as requiring Fourier infrastructure; needed by the Borromean\nsqueeze to evaluate the continuum functional at `x = 3/4` as\n`8·Cl₂(π/2)`. (bean qou-jor3) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.tendsto_master_error","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.tendsto_master_error","kind":"theorem","line":1370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L1370-L1411","doc":"**Saddle brick E5c-5 — the master error vanishes (sorry-free).** The\nk-independent E5c-4 master error\n`E(N) = |F(π/N)| + (π/N)|f(π/N)| + 7·(π/N)(|f(π/N)| + log 2)` tends to\n`0` as `N → ∞`: the Clausen-primitive term by continuity of `clausen` at\n`0` (the E4d-1 route), the first-grid term by E4d-2, and the `log 2` cell\nterm by `π/N → 0`. Together with E5c-4 this squeezes the scaled Kashaev\nlog-sum onto the Clausen primitive uniformly in `k`. (bean qou-2cmk) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.abs_deviation_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.abs_deviation_le","kind":"theorem","line":1254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L1254-L1368","doc":"**Saddle brick E5c-4 — the `π/2`-stitch: all-`k` uniform deviation\n(sorry-free).** For `N ≥ 4` and every `1 ≤ k ≤ N − 1`, the scaled Kashaev\nlog-sum deviates from the Clausen primitive `F(kπ/N) = −clausen(2kπ/N)/2`\nby at most the k-INDEPENDENT master error\n`E(N) = |F(π/N)| + (π/N)|f(π/N)| + 7c`, `c = (π/N)(|f(π/N)| + log 2)`:\nthe rising range `k + 1 ≤ ⌊N/2⌋` by E5c-1 (cost `E₁ = |F| + h|f| + c`),\nthe two mid indices `k = ⌊N/2⌋, ⌊N/2⌋+1` straddling `π/2` by one E5c-4a\nstep each (`+2c` per step), and the falling range `k ≥ ⌊N/2⌋+2` by gluing\nthe prefix at `⌊N/2⌋+1` to E5c-3 (`+2c`). Every summand of `E(N)` tends\nto `0` as `N → ∞` — the E5c-5 brick. (bean qou-xqae) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.abs_deviation_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.abs_deviation_succ","kind":"theorem","line":1197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L1197-L1252","doc":"**Saddle brick E5c-4a — one-cell extension step (sorry-free).** If the\nscaled Kashaev log-sum deviates from the Clausen primitive by at most `B`\nat index `k`, it deviates by at most `B + 2c` at `k + 1`, where\n`c = (π/N)(|f(π/N)| + log 2)`: the new summand is charged one `c` via\nE5c-2 and the new cell `[kπ/N, (k+1)π/N]` one `c` via the crude cell\nbound. Works anywhere in the mirror window (`k + 1 ≤ N − 1`) — this is\nthe step that stitches the rising (E5c-1) and falling (E5c-3) halves\nacross `π/2`. (bean qou-xqae) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.abs_falling_deviation_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.abs_falling_deviation_le","kind":"theorem","line":1141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L1141-L1195","doc":"**Saddle brick E5c-3 — falling uniform deviation (sorry-free).** For any\nfalling window `[mπ/N, kπ/N] ⊆ [π/2, π−π/N]`, the scaled block log-sum\ndeviates from the Clausen-primitive difference by at most the\n(m,k)-INDEPENDENT error `2·(π/N)(|f(π/N)| + log 2)` — E4e-ii sandwich +\nF-bridge, boundary terms charged to E5c-2. (bean qou-emex) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.abs_rising_deviation_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.abs_rising_deviation_le","kind":"theorem","line":1081,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L1081-L1139","doc":"**Saddle brick E5c-1 — rising uniform deviation (sorry-free).** For every\n`k` in the rising range `(k+1)π/N ≤ π/2`, the scaled Kashaev log-sum\ndeviates from the Clausen primitive `F(kπ/N) = −clausen(2kπ/N)/2` by at most\nthe k-INDEPENDENT master error\n`E₁(N) = |F(π/N)| + (π/N)|f(π/N)| + (π/N)(|f(π/N)| + log 2)`\n— assembled from the E4e-i sandwich, the F-bridge, and the crude bound on\nthe single overshoot cell `[kπ/N, (k+1)π/N]`. Every E₁ summand → 0 by E4d.\n(bean qou-bnge) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.integral_log_sin_window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.integral_log_sin_window","kind":"theorem","line":1069,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L1069-L1079","doc":"**E5 F-bridge (sorry-free).** The log-sine integral over any window as a\nClausen-primitive difference: `∫_a^b = F(b) − F(a)` with\n`F(x) = −clausen(2x)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.abs_log_two_sin_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.abs_log_two_sin_le","kind":"theorem","line":1052,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L1052-L1067","doc":"**E5c-2 — pointwise integrand bound (sorry-free).** On the mirror window\n`[h, π−h]`, `|log(2 sin u)| ≤ |log(2 sin h)| + log 2` — ceiling + floor\ncombined. (bean qou-n8d0) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.abs_integral_log_sin_cell_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.abs_integral_log_sin_cell_le","kind":"theorem","line":1021,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L1021-L1050","doc":"**E5b crude cell bound (sorry-free).** For any window `[a, b] ⊆ [h, π−h]`,\nthe log-sine integral is at most `(b−a)·(|f(h)| + log 2)` in absolute value —\nthe boundary-cell control the E5 stitch charges to the master error term.\n(bean qou-sho7) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.log_two_sin_ge_boundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.log_two_sin_ge_boundary","kind":"theorem","line":1004,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L1004-L1019","doc":"**E5b floor (sorry-free).** On the mirror-symmetric window `[h, π−h]`\n(with `0 < h ≤ π/2`), the unimodal log-sine integrand is at least its\ncommon boundary value `f(h)`: by monotonicity up to `π/2` and the\nreflection `sin(π−u) = sin u` beyond. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.log_two_sin_le_log_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.log_two_sin_le_log_two","kind":"theorem","line":996,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L996-L1002","doc":"**E5b ceiling (sorry-free).** The log-sine integrand never exceeds `log 2`\non `(0, π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.integral_le_sum_log_sin_falling_Icc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.integral_le_sum_log_sin_falling_Icc","kind":"theorem","line":970,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L970-L994","doc":"**Saddle brick E4e-ii, lower (sorry-free).** Falling-half Kashaev-indexed\nlower bound with explicit boundary terms: on `[mπ/N, kπ/N] ⊆ [π/2, π)`,\n`∫_{mπ/N}^{kπ/N} ≤ (π/N)·Σ_{j∈Icc (m+1) k} + (π/N)·f(mπ/N) − (π/N)·f(kπ/N)`\n— the E5 assembly bounds the two boundary terms (near `π/2` the integrand is\nat most `log 2`; near `π` it mirrors the E4d singular cell by\n`sin(π−u) = sin u`). (bean qou-x5mg) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.sum_log_sin_le_integral_falling_Icc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.sum_log_sin_le_integral_falling_Icc","kind":"theorem","line":947,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L947-L968","doc":"**Saddle brick E4e-ii, upper (sorry-free).** Falling-half Kashaev-indexed\nupper bound: on `[mπ/N, kπ/N] ⊆ [π/2, π)`,\n`(π/N)·Σ_{j∈Icc (m+1) k} log(2sin(jπ/N)) ≤ ∫_{mπ/N}^{kπ/N}` — the falling\nsums are right-endpoint sums of an antitone integrand. (bean qou-x5mg) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.sum_Ico_eq_add_sum_Icc_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.sum_Ico_eq_add_sum_Icc_sub","kind":"theorem","line":930,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L930-L945","doc":"**E4e decomposition helper (sorry-free).** The left-endpoint sum over\n`Ico m k` in terms of the Kashaev index set: for `m ≤ k`,\n`Σ_{Ico m k} g = g(m) + Σ_{Icc (m+1) k} g − g(k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.sum_Icc_succ_eq_sum_Ico","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.sum_Icc_succ_eq_sum_Ico","kind":"theorem","line":912,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L912-L928","doc":"**E4e reindex helper (sorry-free).** Shifting a sum from the Kashaev index\nset `Icc (m+1) k` to right-endpoint form over `Ico m k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.integral_le_sum_log_sin_Icc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.integral_le_sum_log_sin_Icc","kind":"theorem","line":873,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L873-L910","doc":"**Saddle brick E4e-i, lower (sorry-free).** The Kashaev-indexed rising-half\nlower bound: `∫_{π/N}^{kπ/N} + (π/N)·log(2sin(π/N)) ≤ (π/N)·Σ_{j∈Icc 1 k}` —\nE4c-lower plus the split-off first grid term (whose scaled value vanishes\nby E4d-2). (bean qou-x5mg) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.sum_log_sin_le_integral_Icc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.sum_log_sin_le_integral_Icc","kind":"theorem","line":861,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L861-L871","doc":"**Saddle brick E4e-i, upper (sorry-free).** The Kashaev-indexed rising-half\nupper bound: `(π/N)·Σ_{j∈Icc 1 k} log(2sin(jπ/N)) ≤ ∫_{π/N}^{(k+1)π/N}` —\nE4c-upper with the grid `Ico 1 (k+1)` rewritten to the Kashaev index set\n`Icc 1 k`. (bean qou-x5mg) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.tendsto_first_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.tendsto_first_term","kind":"theorem","line":786,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L786-L859","doc":"**Saddle brick E4d-2 (sorry-free).** The scaled first grid term\n`(π/N)·log(2 sin(π/N)) → 0`: squeezed between the primitive differences\n`∫₀^{π/N} ≤ (π/N)·f(π/N) ≤ ∫_{π/N}^{2π/N}` (monotonicity of the integrand\nnear `0`), both of which vanish by E4d-1 — no `x·log x` special-function\nlimit needed. (bean qou-x5mg) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.tendsto_integral_cell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.tendsto_integral_cell","kind":"theorem","line":768,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L768-L784","doc":"**Saddle brick E4d-1 (sorry-free).** The cell integral `∫₀^{C·π/N}` of the\nlog-sine vanishes as `N → ∞` — the singular first cell contributes nothing\nin the limit. Via E4a + continuity of `clausen` at `0`. (bean qou-x5mg) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.clausen_two_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.clausen_two_pi","kind":"theorem","line":762,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L762-L766","doc":"`clausen(2π) = 0` — the right endpoint, by the closed-interval bridge and\n`Cl₂(2π) = 0`. Equivalently `∫₀^π log(2 sin u) du = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.clausen_eqOn_Icc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.clausen_eqOn_Icc","kind":"theorem","line":754,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L754-L760","doc":"The series↔integral bridge extends to the CLOSED interval `[0, 2π]` by\ncontinuity of both sides (`Set.EqOn.closure`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.clausen_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.clausen_zero","kind":"theorem","line":750,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L750-L752","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.continuous_clausen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.continuous_clausen","kind":"theorem","line":742,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L742-L748","doc":"**`clausen` is continuous (E4d support, sorry-free).** The primitive of an\neverywhere interval-integrable function is continuous\n(`intervalIntegral.continuous_primitive`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.intervalIntegrable_log_two_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.intervalIntegrable_log_two_sin","kind":"theorem","line":731,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L731-L740","doc":"The unhalved log-sine integrand is interval-integrable (transport of the\nhalved version through `t = 2u`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.integral_le_sum_log_sin_falling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.integral_le_sum_log_sin_falling","kind":"theorem","line":695,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L695-L729","doc":"**Saddle brick E4c, falling-half upper bound (sorry-free).** On a window\n`[k₁π/N, k₂π/N] ⊆ [π/2, π)`, the integral is dominated by `π/N` times the\nleft-endpoint log-sine sum — library `AntitoneOn.integral_le_sum_Ico`,\nsame transport. (bean qou-x5mg) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.sum_log_sin_le_integral_falling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.sum_log_sin_le_integral_falling","kind":"theorem","line":655,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L655-L693","doc":"**Saddle brick E4c, falling-half lower bound (sorry-free).** On a window\n`[k₁π/N, k₂π/N] ⊆ [π/2, π)`, the right-endpoint log-sine sum is dominated\nby the integral — library `AntitoneOn.sum_le_integral_Ico`, transported by\n`u = v·π/N`. (bean qou-x5mg) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.antitoneOn_log_two_sin_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.antitoneOn_log_two_sin_mul","kind":"theorem","line":642,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L642-L653","doc":"**E4c helper, falling half (sorry-free).** On the unit grid `[c₁, c₂]`, the\nrescaled `v ↦ log(2 sin(v·h))` inherits E4b's antitonicity when\n`π/2 ≤ c₁·h` and `c₂·h < π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.sum_log_sin_le_integral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.sum_log_sin_le_integral","kind":"theorem","line":600,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L600-L640","doc":"**Saddle brick E4c, rising-half upper bound (sorry-free).** `π/N` times the\nleft-endpoint log-sine sum `Σ_{j=1}^{k}` is dominated by the integral over\nthe widened window `[π/N, (k+1)π/N]` — library\n`MonotoneOn.sum_le_integral_Ico`, same transport. (bean qou-x5mg) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.integral_le_sum_log_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.integral_le_sum_log_sin","kind":"theorem","line":561,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L561-L598","doc":"**Saddle brick E4c, rising-half lower bound (sorry-free).** On the shifted\nwindow `[π/N, kπ/N]` inside the rising half, the integral is dominated by\n`π/N` times the right-endpoint log-sine sum — library\n`MonotoneOn.integral_le_sum_Ico` on the unit grid, transported by the\nchange of variables `u = v·π/N`. (bean qou-x5mg) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.monotoneOn_log_two_sin_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.monotoneOn_log_two_sin_mul","kind":"theorem","line":549,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L549-L559","doc":"**E4c helper (sorry-free).** On the unit grid `[1, c]`, the rescaled\n`v ↦ log(2 sin(v·h))` inherits E4b's monotonicity when `c·h ≤ π/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.antitoneOn_log_two_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.antitoneOn_log_two_sin","kind":"theorem","line":531,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L531-L547","doc":"**Saddle brick E4b, falling half (sorry-free).** `log(2 sin)` is antitone on\n`[π/2, π)` — by the reflection `sin u = sin(π − u)` and the rising half. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.monotoneOn_log_two_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.monotoneOn_log_two_sin","kind":"theorem","line":513,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L513-L529","doc":"**Saddle brick E4b, rising half (sorry-free).** `log(2 sin)` is monotone on\n`(0, π/2]` (strict monotonicity of `sin` + monotonicity of `log` on\npositives). The point `0` is excluded: `log(2 sin 0) = log 0 = 0` exceeds\nnearby negative values under Mathlib's `log 0 = 0` convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.integral_log_two_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.integral_log_two_sin","kind":"theorem","line":496,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L496-L511","doc":"**Saddle brick E4a (sorry-free).** The log-sine integral is the Clausen\nprimitive under `t = 2u`: `∫₀^a log(2 sin u) du = −clausen(2a)/2` — the\ncontinuum limit the Kashaev Riemann sums converge to (bean qou-x5mg). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Cl_2_pi_div_three_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Cl_2_pi_div_three_pos","kind":"theorem","line":485,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L485-L494","doc":"**`Cl₂(π/3) > 0` (saddle brick E3b, sorry-free).** Transported from the\nintegral side through the machine-proved bridge `clausen_eq_series`. This is\nthe strict positivity that makes the Kashaev saddle value\n`2 Cl₂(π/3) = Vol(4₁)` a genuine maximum (the `θ = 5π/3` minimum of `Cl₂`\nequals `−Cl₂(π/3) < 0 <` the endpoint values `0`; bean qou-yzs2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.clausen_pi_div_three_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.clausen_pi_div_three_pos","kind":"theorem","line":461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L461-L483","doc":"**`clausen(π/3) > 0` (saddle brick E3b, integral side, sorry-free).** On\n`(0, π/3)` the integrand `-log(2 sin(t/2))` is strictly positive\n(`2 sin(t/2) < 2 sin(π/6) = 1` by strict monotonicity of `sin`), so the\nintegral is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Cl_2_two_pi_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Cl_2_two_pi_sub","kind":"theorem","line":445,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L445-L459","doc":"**Antisymmetry of `Cl_2` about `π` (saddle brick E2, sorry-free).**\n`Cl_2(2π − θ) = −Cl_2(θ)`: termwise `sin((k+1)(2π−θ)) = −sin((k+1)θ)` by\n`2π`-periodicity (`Real.sin_int_mul_two_pi_sub`). Locates the minimum of\n`Cl_2` on `(0,2π)` at `θ = 5π/3` with value `−Cl_2(π/3)` — the value the\nKashaev saddle max `−2Cl_2(2πx)` attains at `x = 5/6`, feeding the\nexistence/value program for `VolumeConjecture41` (bean qou-yrog). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.clausen_eq_series","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.clausen_eq_series","kind":"theorem","line":438,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L438-L443","doc":"**Series↔integral bridge (sorry-free).** On `(0, 2π)`,\n`∫₀^θ -log(2 sin(t/2)) = ∑ sin(kθ)/k²` — the classical Zagier identity,\nfully machine-proved via `clausen_eqOn_Cl_2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.clausen_eqOn_Cl_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.clausen_eqOn_Cl_2","kind":"theorem","line":421,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L421-L436","doc":"**Reduction (Route-B brick 2, sorry-free).** `clausen` and\n`Cl_2` agree on `(0, 2π)`: both have derivative `-log(2 sin(θ/2))` there\n(`hasDerivAt_clausen`, `hasDerivAt_Cl_2_series`) and agree at the interior\npoint `θ = π` (`clausen_pi`, `Cl_2_pi`), so they are equal on the connected\nopen interval by `eqOn_of_deriv_eq`. This is the constant-pinning machinery\nthat turns the single derivative atom into the full series↔integral bridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.hasDerivAt_Cl_2_series","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.hasDerivAt_Cl_2_series","kind":"theorem","line":390,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L390-L419","doc":"**The atom — CLOSED, sorry-free.** `Cl_2'(θ) = -log(2 sin(θ/2))` on\n`(0, 2π)`: the term-by-term derivative of the Fourier-series Clausen — the\nidentity the filler file deferred to \"Fourier-series infrastructure not in\nMathlib\". Proved by `hasDerivAt_of_tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn` from\n`hasDerivAt_g_r` (brick 4), `tendsto_Cl_2_reg` (brick 1), and\n`tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn_tsum_rpow_cos` (brick 5, the former `hf'`).\nWith this the whole file is sorry-free: the Zagier series↔integral bridge\n(`clausen_eq_series`) and the `Cl_2` derivative are machine-proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn_tsum_rpow_cos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn_tsum_rpow_cos","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L296-L388","doc":"**Assembly brick 5 — `hf'`, the local-uniform convergence (sorry-free).**\nAs `r → 1⁻`, the regularised derivatives `g_r' = ∑ₙ rⁿ cos(n·)/n` converge\nlocally uniformly on `(0, 2π)` to `-log(2 sin(·/2))`. The closing trick: the\nseries equals its closed form `F(r,t) = -log‖1 - r e^{it}‖` (brick 2b), and\n`F` is jointly continuous THROUGH `r = 1` away from `t ∈ 2πℤ` (the only zeros\nof `1 - r e^{it}` for `r > 0`, via `Complex.exp_eq_one_iff`); on a compact\n`K ⊆ (0,2π)` the compact product `[½,3/2] ×ˢ K` gives uniform continuity\n(Heine–Cantor), hence uniform convergence as `r → 1` within `[½,3/2]`. The\nconditional-convergence \"wall\" was an artifact of the series representation —\nno Dirichlet-kernel estimate is needed. (bean qou-6fkd) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.hasDerivAt_g_r","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.hasDerivAt_g_r","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L242-L294","doc":"**Assembly brick 4 (sorry-free)** — term-by-term derivative of the Abel-\nregularised `g_r`. For `|r| < 1`,\n`d/dθ ∑ₙ sin(nθ)/n² · rⁿ = ∑ₙ rⁿ cos(nθ)/n`. Absolute convergence at `r<1`\n(derivative bound `|r|ⁿ`, summable geometric) makes `hasDerivAt_tsum` apply —\nthe conditional-convergence obstruction bites only at `r=1`. (bean qou-7lj2) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.norm_one_sub_exp_ofReal_mul_I","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.norm_one_sub_exp_ofReal_mul_I","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L224-L240","doc":"**Assembly brick 3 (sorry-free)** — the boundary norm identity. For every θ,\n`‖1 - e^{iθ}‖ = 2 |sin(θ/2)|`. Hence the `r→1⁻` limit of brick 2b's closed\nform `-log‖1 - r e^{iθ}‖` is `-log(2 sin(θ/2))` on `(0,2π)` (where\n`sin(θ/2) > 0`) — the boundary log value the atom needs. (bean qou-cdxw) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.tsum_rpow_cos_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.tsum_rpow_cos_div","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L200-L222","doc":"**Assembly brick 2b (sorry-free)** — the real cos-series closed form. For\n`|r| < 1`, `∑ₙ rⁿ cos(nθ)/n = -log‖1 - r e^{iθ}‖`. Real part of brick 2a\n(`hasSum_pow_div_neg_log`) at `w = r e^{iθ}`, using Euler\n(`exp_ofReal_mul_I_re`) and `Complex.log_re`. (bean qou-smve) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.hasSum_pow_div_neg_log","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.hasSum_pow_div_neg_log","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L180-L198","doc":"**Assembly brick 2a (sorry-free)** — the complex log power series at the\nboundary interior: `∑ₙ wⁿ/n = -log(1-w)` for `‖w‖ < 1`. Derived from Mathlib's\n`Complex.hasSum_taylorSeries_log` (`∑ (-1)^{n+1} zⁿ/n = log(1+z)`) at `z = -w`,\nwith the sign algebra `(-1)^{n+1}(-w)ⁿ = -wⁿ`. (bean qou-6r0y) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.clausen_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.clausen_pi","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L148-L178","doc":"**`clausen π = 0` (Route-B brick 2, sorry-free).** The interior agreement\npoint that pins the bridge constant. Change of variables `t = 2x`\n(`integral_comp_div`) reduces to `∫₀^{π/2} log(2 sin x)`, which splits\n*pointwise* on `Ι 0 (π/2)` (there `sin x > 0`) into `log 2 + log sin x`;\nMathlib's `integral_log_sin_zero_pi_div_two = -log2·π/2` then gives\n`(π/2)log2 + (-log2·π/2) = 0`. No a.e. reasoning. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.tendsto_Cl_2_reg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.tendsto_Cl_2_reg","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L125-L146","doc":"**Abel-regularisation of `Cl_2` (assembly brick, sorry-free).** As `x → 1⁻`,\n`∑ₙ (sin(nθ)/n²) xⁿ → Cl_2 θ` — Abel's limit theorem\n(`Real.tendsto_tsum_powerSeries_nhdsWithin_lt`), valid because the\n`sin(nθ)/n²` series converges absolutely at `x = 1`. First brick of the Abel\nroute discharging the atom `hasDerivAt_Cl_2_series`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.continuous_Cl_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.continuous_Cl_2","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L107-L123","doc":"**`Cl_2` is continuous (Route-B support brick, sorry-free).** Weierstrass\nM-test: each term `θ ↦ sin((k+1)θ)/(k+1)²` is continuous and bounded by the\nsummable `1/(k+1)²`. The filler file *asserts* \"the tsum is well-defined and\ncontinuous\" without proof; this discharges it. Needed to pin the constant in\nthe series↔integral bridge (both `clausen` and `Cl_2` → 0 at `θ = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.hasDerivAt_clausen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.hasDerivAt_clausen","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L80-L105","doc":"**Brick 3 — the Clausen derivative (dual-purpose).** For `θ ∈ (0, 2π)`,\n`Cl₂'(θ) = -log(2 sin(θ/2))`. This is the fundamental theorem of calculus\napplied to the interval-integrable, at-`θ`-continuous integrand. It is\n*simultaneously* the derivative `V'(θ)` of the QOU dilog-saddle potential\n`V(θ) = Im Li₂(e^{iθ}) = Cl₂(θ)` — the load-bearing derivative claim of\ncontent block `rem:dilog-saddle-regime`, now Lean-proved. Its zero is the\nsaddle `θ = π/3` (`saddle_critical_point`), giving `Vol(4₁) = 2 Cl₂(π/3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.intervalIntegrable_log_two_sin_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.intervalIntegrable_log_two_sin_half","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L73-L78","doc":"**Integrability of the Clausen integrand.** `t ↦ log(2 sin(t/2))` is\ninterval-integrable on every `a..b`; the log-singularities of `sin` at\nmultiples of `2π` are integrable (`MeromorphicOn.intervalIntegrable_log`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.analyticOnNhd_two_sin_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.analyticOnNhd_two_sin_half","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L60-L71","doc":"`t ↦ 2 sin(t/2)` is analytic (entire) on any real segment — the analytic\nhull the meromorphic-log integrability lemma needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.clausen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.clausen","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/Clausen.lean#L55-L58","doc":"The Clausen function `Cl₂(θ) = ∫₀^θ -log(2 sin(t/2)) dt` (Lobachevsky\nprimitive of `-log(2 sin(·/2))`). Not available in Mathlib. ","signatureChunk":0}]}